Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding (MTP / DFlash / DSpark) — upstream
PR #36186 plus its two DFlash2 prerequisites, rebased onto tag v0.5.18.

Source commits (all MERGED into sgl-project/sglang main):
  c14312a664  [Spec] DFlash2: local convolution + candidate selector (#35371)
  1cf2b8c54d  [Spec] Support quantized target lm_head in the DFlash2 selector (#35496)
  41e7612dee  [Model] Support Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding (#36186)
              merged 2026-08-25T23:43:58Z
Captured 2026-08-28 by cherry-picking the three commits onto v0.5.18 (71de97b264)
in that order and resolving the four residual conflicts (see REBASE NOTES).

WHY THE TWO EXTRA COMMITS. v0.5.18 was tagged 2026-08-22, three days before
#36186 merged, so #36186 alone does NOT apply: it is written against a dflash.py
that already carries DFlash2 (#35371 introduced DFlashGroupedConv, the candidate
selector, _radix_topk and the `prefix=`/conv constructor signatures; #35496 added
is_dense_head_weight and the quantized-lm_head selector path). Applying #36186 by
itself onto v0.5.18 fails 5 of 18 files. With the two prerequisites first, only
four small conflicts remain, all of them main-only drift unrelated to Nemotron.
The two prerequisites are self-contained: they touch dflash.py, dflash_utils.py,
dflash_worker_v2.py, spec_aux_hidden_state.py and one kernels/ops file, nothing
in the config-namespace refactor that dominates the rest of the v0.5.18..main gap.

Target model: nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4 (arch
  NemotronHForCausalLM, hybrid Mamba-2 + MoE + attention, modelopt MIXED_PRECISION
  with W4A16_NVFP4 experts/lm_head) together with its two published external draft
  checkpoints, ...-NVFP4-DSpark (arch Qwen3DSparkModel) and ...-NVFP4-DFlash (arch
  DFlashDraftModel), both W4A16_NVFP4. Serving the TARGET alone needs none of this
  (v0.5.18 already carries the mixed-NVFP4 support from the merged PR #27906);
  this patch is required only for the three speculative decoders. Without it the
  DSPARK/DFLASH paths die at
    model_runner_components/attention_backend_setup.py
    "Model NemotronHForCausalLM implements neither set_dspark_layers_to_capture
     nor set_dflash_layers_to_capture, one of which is required for DFLASH/DSPARK."
  because dflash_use_aux_hidden_state is set unconditionally for the dflash family
  in spec_aux_hidden_state.py::_resolve_dflash_aux_hidden_state and nemotron_h.py
  has no residual-layer capture hook in v0.5.18.
  See roles/k8s_dgx/model_profiles/nvidia-nvidia-nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b-nvfp4.yml.

What it does (16 files; the PR's docs page and its three test files are
intentionally NOT included — everything outside python/sglang/srt and
python/sglang/kernels was dropped during the rebase):
  - models/nemotron_h.py: set_dflash_layers_to_capture + the residual/aux hidden
    state capture the DFlash-family drafts consume. This is THE hook whose absence
    is the hard blocker above (attention_backend_setup falls back to the dflash
    spelling when a model has no set_dspark_layers_to_capture, so this one method
    serves both DSPARK and DFLASH).
  - models/dflash.py: Nemotron-3.5 draft layout — the draft's own
    VocabParallelEmbedding (upstream drafts borrow the target's), ReplicatedLinear
    fc with a packed-weight-aware shape check, weight prefixes, attention sinks
    (which REQUIRE --speculative-draft-attention-backend trtllm_mha and raise
    otherwise), plus the DFlash2 conv/selector machinery from the prerequisites.
  - models/dspark.py: Nemotron-3.5 DSpark Markov fixup head + bonus-anchor
    handling; quantized-lm_head aware candidate projection.
  - layers/quantization/modelopt_quant.py: ModelOpt W4A16 NVFP4 for the DRAFT
    checkpoints (both drafts ship quant_algo W4A16_NVFP4, group_size 16).
  - arg_groups/overrides.py: the Nemotron-H resolver that picks target/draft
    attention backends on Blackwell WITHOUT overriding an explicit user choice.
    This is why the model profile leaves attention_backend empty.
  - arg_groups/speculative_hook.py, speculative/dspark_components/*: derive the
    DSpark anchor sampling and the Nemotron Markov layout from the already-loaded
    draft config; no new ServerArgs knob is added by the PR.
  - speculative/dflash_utils.py: is_nemotron_35_draft_config + the DFlash2 helpers.
  - model_executor/model_runner.py, model_runner_components/spec_aux_hidden_state.py,
    server_args.py: small plumbing for the above.
  - kernels/ops/speculative/dflash.py: the DFlash2 kernel op (from #35371).

REBASE NOTES (four conflicts, all resolved toward v0.5.18 semantics):
  1. models/dspark.py — pure import addition (ReplicatedLinear,
     should_apply_lm_head_quant_method). Both symbols DO exist in v0.5.18
     (layers/linear.py, layers/logits_processor.py:1035). Took both sides.
  2. speculative/dflash_worker_v2.py and
     speculative/dspark_components/dspark_draft.py — upstream wraps the embedding
     module in unwrap_lora_layer(). That helper (sglang.srt.lora.layers) does NOT
     exist in v0.5.18 and is NOT part of #36186: it sits on the CONTEXT side of
     both upstream hunks, i.e. it is unrelated main-only LoRA plumbing. DROPPED
     the wrapper, kept the PR's actual change (draft-owned embeddings via
     _resolve_dflash_embedding_module / self.draft_model.embed_tokens).
  3. speculative/dspark_components/dspark_config.py — upstream renames
     read_draft_checkpoint_gamma to read_draft_checkpoint_config (the new name IS
     needed: speculative_hook.py calls it) and switches the four field reads to
     arg_groups.overrides.resolved_view(). resolved_view exists in v0.5.18 but
     does not cover these fields there; the plain server_args attributes are the
     resolving values on this tag. Took the rename, kept the direct reads, and
     left an in-file NOTE saying to restore resolved_view() on a newer base.
  Verified: `git apply --check -p1` (strict, no fuzz) and `patch --dry-run -p1`
  (what the container build runs) are BOTH clean against pristine v0.5.18, and
  pyflakes reports no undefined names across all 16 changed files.

